1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,700
Over 12,000 km apart,
two nations.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:05,300
One war over a few
windswept islands.

3
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:08,400
The Falkland Islands —
Las Malvinas to Argentines

4
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:10,500
About 480 km from
Argentina's coast

5
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:12,300
British since 1833

6
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:15,200
2 April 1982
Argentina invades

7
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:17,500
A day later:
South Georgia seized

8
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:21,400
Britain sends a
task force south

9
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:24,000
26 April:
South Georgia retaken

10
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:27,200
21 May: British troops
land at San Carlos

11
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:30,000
Advance on
Stanley

12
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:32,800
14 June:
Argentina surrenders

13
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:35,000
The war lasted
74 days

14
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:38,200
649 Argentine and
255 British servicemen

15
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:41,400
Plus 3 islanders
killed

16
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:45,800
2013 referendum:
99.8% stay British

17
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:49,200
Argentina still claims
the islands

18
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:51,800
Britain says the
islanders decide

19
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:53,400
A dispute still
unsettled
